{
  "_comment": [
    "Wan2.2 I2V VBench gate (test_module/_test_common/vbench_gate.py), per the validation plan's release CI.",
    "Each run is compared with the GPU run made the same way (drift: Cache-DiT on -> refs/r2/tt, off -> refs/r1), and a cached run also with refs/r1 (budget: the expected cost of caching).",
    "VBench: a gated dimension fails if TT's mean is more than tolerance_pct below the reference's over the same clips. TT scoring higher never fails. dynamic_degree and camera_motion are pass/fail per clip, so they are reported, not gated.",
    "Output (drift comparison only, per resolution): a clip fails if its mean LPIPS exceeds max_clip_lpips; the run fails if its mean PSNR, SSIM or LPIPS over the calibrated clips moves more than mean_margin from the calibration's mean over the same clips.",
    "480p calibration: refs/r1 from tt-shield run 40839687590 (Cache-DiT off, the ci subset's 10 clips at 832x480); refs/r2/tt from 40854021902 (on, the all subset's 40 clips at 832x480, which repeat 40839683835's 10 to the digit). BH Galaxy at 480p, tt-metal 9b40b665. Worst clip LPIPS 0.402 and 0.485; max_clip_lpips 0.55 was set at about 0.1 over the first 10 clips' worst.",
    "refs/r2/tt's 480x832 clips (10) and 720p calibration (15 clips at 1280x720 and 720x1280): a local release eval on BH Galaxy, Cache-DiT on, 2026-11-05, image ghcr.io/tenstorrent/tt-shield/tt-media-inference-server:0.26.1-ea24a5429f153f183704a8bdcf65a88026d38f06-de55f31-127107813048, tt-inference-server 0af398261, x264 preset ultrafast; its 832x480 clips repeat the calibration's means to 4 digits. 720p worst clip LPIPS 0.539 (vbi2v_0790_720x1280), so max_clip_lpips 0.64 is about 0.1 over it. 720p has no refs/r1 calibration yet (needs a Cache-DiT off run), so a cache-off run's 720p clips are checked only against max_clip_lpips.",
    "Change any value only with review."
  ],
